Please find attached weekly performance report of DME.

I. Sales & Marketing
1) Market Situation and Competiton  Activities
TPS/TAS Market volume has no significant changes as compared to last week
Due to the ongoing market conditions for this trade , carriers in this market are not confident to announce rate increase
AES     Market volume not picked up for NWC & MED
Major carriers MSK/SAF /UASC / Hapag Lloyd /CMA  have withdrawn GRI in this market in view of the slow market conditions
Cargo moving to Egypt has slowed down due to restriction on visa issuance to Egyptian traders
IAS (Outbound)  IAS Outbound market volumes are stable
Metal Scrap movements to India has increased due to the price fluctuation ,buyers benefiting nbetter price from India as compared to F.E / S.E.A
Vehicle movements which is one of the major commodity to the Far East have slowed down due to delay of 2014 models from the manufacturers
IAS ( Inbound ) Market volume not improved vs traditional peak
FOB market showing rate drop from both Far East and South East Asia, current frt levels are $650 ~ $700 to base ports
Others  GPDC will be loading from Jubail eff 2014 tender period, which will affect our loading due to limited space availability

